@@ -22,3 +22,12 @@ apply in order. It throws an `Error` if the patch is invalid (not an array, unkn
 invalid `path`, `from` or `value`; a `value` must be JSON: no `NaN`, `Infinity`, `undefined`, functions or class instances) or if an operation fails (target missing, array index out of range,
 `move` into its own child, failed `test`); a failed patch returns nothing, so it is all-or-nothing.
 Removing the whole document is rejected. `test` compares by JSON equality (member order is ignored).
+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Merge Patch to a target
+document and returns the merged document as a new value; neither argument is mutated and the result
+shares no structure with them. A patch that is not an object replaces the target; an object patch is
+merged member by member, and a `null` member removes that member from the target. Arrays are replaced,
+not merged, so `null` inside an array is kept. A `null` member of the patch cannot set a value to
+`null`. It throws an `Error` if `target` or `patch` is not JSON (see `applyPatch` for what counts).
